  "body": "# G5: triggered digital waveform replay\n\nTwo 20-word programs reuse the unchanged G4-qualified chip as a triggered\nsource of irregular digital stimulus. The timing-fault program moves one\nselected rising edge by two clocks, while every later output transition and\nthe final release retain their original timing. At the assumed 50 MHz clock\nthe shift is 40 ns; this is a digital schedule conversion, not a new frequency\nor physical pad measurement.\n\n[Qualified source 66743b6](https://github.com/KG-khangelani/protocol-emulator-asic/tree/66743b60b93508d2f00f23fa2cc2ac7db244bc3a)\npasses [run 43697229433](https://github.com/KG-khangelani/protocol-emulator-asic/actions/runs/43697229433):\n\n- 21 public-pin cases in each of Icarus and Verilator, including five expected\n  rejections; a separate clean clone reproduces every record and trace byte.\n- All 366 producing inputs match the committed source. Both programs occupy\n  80 bytes; only WAIT words 9 and 11 differ.\n- Trigger phase/boundary, timeout cleanup, pin ownership, disabled-clock\n  stretching, actual corrupted load-byte rejection and reload recovery pass.\n- The existing thirteen UART/SPI/I2C examples retain their bytes and pass all\n  55 public cases per simulator, including fifteen expected rejections.\n- Retained evidence replay passes, and five deliberately rehashed bad-evidence\n  controls are rejected. Native Windows and Linux produce identical compiled\n  program artifacts.\n\nStart with the [example guide](https://github.com/KG-khangelani/protocol-emulator-asic/blob/main/docs/waveform-replay.md).\nThe software bundle supplies the standalone assembler, both readable sources,\neight compiled artifacts and independent checker tests. The original CI ZIP\npreserves the actual qualification and clean reproduction. Their manifest and\n`g5-SHA256SUMS` bind the downloadable bytes. Publication verification is\nrecorded separately in E0048 after downloads are checked.\n\nAll twenty physical inputs remain identical to\n[stable v0.1.0](https://github.com/KG-khangelani/protocol-emulator-asic/releases/tag/v0.1.0).\nIts physical reports, layout archives and submission packet remain the hardware\nreference. This release adds a software example; it does not claim new physical\nqualification, fabricated silicon, an analog glitch generator, unrestricted\nasynchronous capture, a new architecture or completed owner teach-back.\n\nThe initial unsupported comment syntax and unavailable local Docker engine\nare retained in E0048. Correcting only the comments left every instruction,\nexpected trace and investigation limit unchanged. No competition entry has\nbeen submitted.\n\nVerified workbench: `ghcr.io/kg-khangelani/protocol-emulator-asic-workbench@sha256:977a4dc20fe558bb84d941b5aa572d5f456866660ea6a2c4f3a9badd87f7811e`\n\nPublication checks: https://github.com/KG-khangelani/protocol-emulator-asic/actions/runs/43698444537\n",
